{"title":"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(FLT,_CRT,_Inequalities)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (FLT, CRT, Inequalities)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Brute_Force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Brute Force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Cheese)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Cheese)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8_(Guesswork_or_Bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8 (Guesswork or Bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_9_(Guess,_only_if_you_have_no_time)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 9 (Guess, only if you have no time)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Remark\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>One of Euler's conjectures was disproved in the 1960s by three American mathematicians when they showed there was a positive integer such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/143026fa63a7ae20a66ec8c720201f4b53302ba9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[133^5+110^5+84^5+27^5=n^{5}.\\]\" width=\"232\" height=\"17\" /> Find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28FLT.2C_CRT.2C_Inequalities.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(FLT,_CRT,_Inequalities)\">Solution 1 (FLT, CRT, Inequalities)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (FLT, CRT, Inequalities)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Taking the given equation modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/f/01fbbab3253662f64c35a31b865ee26aaa0a7657.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/4/21415a2eb558eb7c199a0382fcd50cbeda9299fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> respectively, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/b/c3b5022b9e6f63753fbd94ba8ab7a0684825fcc8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} n^5&amp;\\equiv0\\pmod{2}, \\\\ n^5&amp;\\equiv0\\pmod{3}, \\\\ n^5&amp;\\equiv4\\pmod{5}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"137\" height=\"75\" />\nBy either <b>Fermat's Little Theorem (FLT)</b> or inspection, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27ec3a2ed938fc272320718558ef0beb72e628c9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} n&amp;\\equiv0\\pmod{2}, \\\\ n&amp;\\equiv0\\pmod{3}, \\\\ n&amp;\\equiv4\\pmod{5}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"130\" height=\"68\" />\nBy either the <b>Chinese Remainder Theorem (CRT)</b> or inspection, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/5/d75ef05c603d21628bc73cc6120f53e80a4196a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\equiv24\\pmod{30}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"138\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>It is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53b7cf1405767b60d84461fe35f9fd7dd1562066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;133,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"17\" /> so the possible values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/6/24696c94bb5c2aacf0057016b4b42183309b56ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144,174,204,\\ldots.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"17\" /> Note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/9/53990f87f1d809d1009fc08c063adf3c11e05cc3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} n^5&amp;=133^5+110^5+84^5+27^5 \\\\ &amp;&lt;133^5+110^5+(84+27)^5 \\\\ &amp;=133^5+110^5+111^5 \\\\ &amp;&lt;3\\cdot133^5, \\end{align*}\" width=\"234\" height=\"102\" />\nfrom which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/066592f63b8bac165fc9478a7a988556cc4d9887.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{n}{133}\\right)^5&lt;3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"100\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/2/602c08ec0ee62e7698445bd4c06e2ce01391389d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq174,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"17\" /> then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/8515cf0ac98d1c1e0624f7cad903a666a1683a4a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\left(\\frac{n}{133}\\right)^5&amp;&gt;1.3^5 \\\\ &amp;=1.3^2\\cdot1.3^2\\cdot1.3 \\\\ &amp;&gt;1.6\\cdot1.6\\cdot1.3 \\\\ &amp;=2.56\\cdot1.3 \\\\ &amp;&gt;2.5\\cdot1.2 \\\\ &amp;=3, \\end{align*}\" width=\"191\" height=\"161\" />\nwhich arrives at a contradiction. Therefore, we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/f/a8f83dec15ec8b46e2915ec49721494565ccc53c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=\\boxed{144}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"81\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even, since the LHS consists of two odd and two even numbers. By Fermat's Little Theorem, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/b/cabf77bca1a67fa09a6f3087221f349605359600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^5\\equiv n\\pmod{5}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"21\" /> Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/1/2b1df66c5f4fb136139934ac01e1f99816282b15.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n\\equiv3+0+4+2\\equiv4\\pmod{5}.\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"18\" />\nContinuing, we examine the equation modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f885f96d2fb7e65f800de4ff71d7dcd0a5d2db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4c6715834530112be1c4e9f277a79fc6f63ce06.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n\\equiv1-1+0+0\\equiv0\\pmod{3}.\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"18\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divisible by three and leaves a remainder of four when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b835f2c6c592edc4583ce996f86bcc0d07ca8da5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> It is obvious that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53b7cf1405767b60d84461fe35f9fd7dd1562066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;133,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"17\" /> so the only possibilities are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/a/fdaff0fd3a4cf5c4fd55293d82c8216d24a28b5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/9/b59584282cd25c98b97f77bea0e599f76bad1684.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 174.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"69\" height=\"16\" /> It quickly becomes apparent that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9a1bf1111b9288bbee8699ee4e9503017e9a42f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$174$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> is much too large, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/4/374cda5d5c55afb5ad0be6643f5b462d33a0c07c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{144}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~Azjps (Solution)\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM (Reformatting)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can cheat a little bit and approximate, since we are dealing with such large numbers. As above, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/c/1bc8d6132572940d2020e9240fdcc5d1a4bd7dd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^5\\equiv n\\pmod{5},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"21\" /> and it is easy to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/6/ea61fba8dc966d526f4c3b358523a662f7a6c8f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^5\\equiv n\\pmod 2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"21\" /> Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/9/539c25171c1324c223cd8177ad1f1c959c6e969d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$133^5+110^5+84^5+27^5\\equiv 3+0+4+7\\equiv 4\\pmod{10},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"436\" height=\"21\" /> so the last digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb15a16cca90d201094265ee529e9e2cfb113de8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>We notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/d/e9d15e28b12427c81e3da98c369f05920b40d987.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$133,110,84,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1051e7d41ec0b8bd688a872be17538413f4ee97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are all very close or equal to multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/f/3afdbc1109a0d51befd8c26e6fbabc35f82e82c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27.$\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" /> We can rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/e/5bea4b4225810d06cab4ca9c250418bbcafec42d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^5$\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> as approximately equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/6/6f605fa352b937a1389c9bc62e90b8e4535b04ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27^5(5^5+4^5+3^5+1^5) = 27^5(4393).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"280\" height=\"21\" /> This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/1/511f7484de66420d93af08b05f7117b6860600e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n^5}{27^5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"31\" height=\"41\" /> must be close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/5/285985a2dc66013d1b882c962f948cdd7b00e726.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4393.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/9/489263c8336e32dbda8c2160060f5aacb822c9e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$134$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> will obviously be too small, so we try <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50ff9540650f0f95f80da2f6692fc8ee413e2eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/0/2d0b0e80672e19acf90e83e812835b366486eee0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{144}{27}\\right)^5=\\left(\\frac{16}{3}\\right)^5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"155\" height=\"48\" /> Bashing through the division, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/486273d92df1b099d4125412fe7b1d72c7cfcdf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1048576}{243}\\approx 4315,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"135\" height=\"38\" /> which is very close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/5/285985a2dc66013d1b882c962f948cdd7b00e726.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4393.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> It is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/6/88624e088523d025e8e29f3fbcdd2a812dfdf1e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$154$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> will not give any closer of an answer, given the rate that fifth powers grow, so we can safely assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/4/a842c2b8241b1784706e13c86f350656b7208be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{144}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" /> is the answer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In this solution we take advantage of the large numbers and utilize parity properties to give us a very good guess at the answer. The units digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/b/2bb58f617e2d92c3de3762233f95f44c4a5dfb0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$133^5, 110^5, 84^5, 27^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"20\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/c/aacd5bb8dd79908fd379f0b15ff911d3736a58be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3, 0, 4, 7,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"17\" /> respectively, so the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/e/5bea4b4225810d06cab4ca9c250418bbcafec42d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^5$\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb15a16cca90d201094265ee529e9e2cfb113de8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> This tells us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even. Since we are dealing with enormous numbers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> should not be that far from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef10596833147c85fba8f74c9a017239e71c5c88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$133.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />'s units digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/6/2a6346c497ac93fc882a000fb106d6e31b085be5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 2, 4, 6,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/1/bb13a1ea7b9fd6892ebe9599c3587aa68288c873.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> When to the power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/4/21415a2eb558eb7c199a0382fcd50cbeda9299fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> they each give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/6/2a6346c497ac93fc882a000fb106d6e31b085be5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 2, 4, 6,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as the units digits. This further clues us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> ends in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb15a16cca90d201094265ee529e9e2cfb113de8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> \n</p><p>Clearly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53b7cf1405767b60d84461fe35f9fd7dd1562066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;133,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"17\" /> so we start with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/18120808c2e0aac1820400d11e3ea0c20fd23e19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$134.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> Now we need a way of distinguishing between numbers with units digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb15a16cca90d201094265ee529e9e2cfb113de8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> We can do this by finding the last three digits for each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/2/c3238ab176b78fe2b1cd483df64ab7b37099cab4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$133^5, 110^5, 84^5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12598fcda6b0d2adcd192ef00d60b107c5c078f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27^5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"20\" /> which is not that difficult. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/a/bcab9dd2e1a55d07fd4b57dfa36ba4a6270f5b87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$133^5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/5/80548742a2d5af410915904f14ba1fa04d3a3aaf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 133^5&amp;=133^2\\cdot133^2\\cdot133 \\\\ &amp;\\equiv689\\cdot689\\cdot133 \\\\ &amp;\\equiv721\\cdot133 \\\\ &amp;\\equiv893\\pmod{1000}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"197\" height=\"95\" />\nBy the same reasoning, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/e/bee0def8ace5518fb050feda5407f2d435394245.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} n^5&amp;=133^5+110^5+84^5+27^5 \\\\ &amp;\\equiv893+0+424+907 \\\\ &amp;\\equiv224\\pmod{1000}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"228\" height=\"70\" />\nNote that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6fef0f725cbeb15bc0bdbb49e5e0de45e4a5c8e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 134^5&amp;\\equiv424\\pmod{1000}, \\\\ 144^5&amp;\\equiv224\\pmod{1000}, \\\\ 154^5&amp;\\equiv024\\pmod{1000}, \\\\ 164^5&amp;\\equiv824\\pmod{1000}, \\\\ 174^5&amp;\\equiv624\\pmod{1000}, \\\\ 184^5&amp;\\equiv424\\pmod{1000}, \\\\ 194^5&amp;\\equiv224\\pmod{1000}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"198\" height=\"186\" />\nBy observations, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/d/1fdf1027f58b450616b1256a2088cb3d8f39a2f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=194$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> is obviously an overestimate. So, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/f/a8f83dec15ec8b46e2915ec49721494565ccc53c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=\\boxed{144}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"81\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~jackshi2006 (Solution)\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM (Revisions and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/latex.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\LaTeX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> Adjustments)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we take mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on both sides to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/5/fd5b22658b464a283ab30ea25ad8d160e96a2df0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^5\\equiv 0\\pmod{2}\\implies n\\equiv 0\\pmod{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"292\" height=\"21\" />. Mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/f/7efed9a9abaf816af09305c58869ea60d4fab5db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^5\\equiv 0\\pmod{3}\\implies n\\equiv 0\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"292\" height=\"21\" />. Also, mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/d/bfd1edea91f455c19f86467b60720fc7a720ec84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^5\\equiv -1\\pmod{5}\\implies n\\equiv -1\\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"320\" height=\"21\" /> (by FLT). Finally, note that mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d74b3dc9eeb9cf48f9b1775b2ab76be1e19e473b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^5\\equiv 2\\pmod{7}\\implies n^{-1}\\equiv 2\\pmod{7}\\implies n\\equiv 4\\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"475\" height=\"21\" />. Thus,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d1c076cc9d1f04b9eb67dda481a7e6ccaedf5af.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} n&amp;\\equiv 0\\pmod{2}, \\\\ n&amp;\\equiv 0\\pmod{3}, \\\\ n&amp;\\equiv -1\\pmod{5}, \\\\ n&amp;\\equiv 4\\pmod{7}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"144\" height=\"93\" />\nBy CRT, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27c838c87f55e08287f7e7ac55471e0a0917d5ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\equiv 144\\pmod{210}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/e/e7e05e95c21fb8b20a6725645000bfa111c453d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144, 354, ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/291bc7938237f81b17ad6d69918018a60abdb99a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$133^5 + 110^5 + 84^5 + 27^5 &lt; 4\\cdot 133^5 &lt; (2\\cdot 133)^5 &lt; 354^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"425\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/0/8009bd0e31d8adc8666fbf7dfe33109b8d158cbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &lt; 354$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"64\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/c/6eca7c28297e6b10ef77741b5fc71c5321e0c6b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\boxed{144}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"76\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~brainfertilzer\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Brute_Force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Brute_Force)\">Solution 6 (Brute Force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Brute Force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/895c0caa4b5c659a02ab26c6f0c72b972fab20b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^5 = 133^5 + 110^5 + 84^5 +27^5 = 61917364224,\\]\" width=\"357\" height=\"19\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7b7e25c2a218baf4e841d289b45116e1b22fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\sqrt [5]{61917364224} = \\boxed{144}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"221\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Cheese.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Cheese)\">Solution 7 (Cheese)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Cheese)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By approximation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/d/f1d93fb89b4fc551c8f1f62b22b63dccce8b4b95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$110 \\approx \\frac{5}{6}\\cdot133$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/8/9b8af6fbb12360d907f3c7ce3b4f54bad890e6d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$84 \\approx \\frac{7}{11}\\cdot133$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a16ec322f1ba0088fab54b2668abdacf268a2a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23 \\approx \\frac{1}{5}\\cdot133$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"38\" />. Adding the fifth power of each fraction of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/0/9501915f08ed1cf295fdd389481801277bcb2e94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$133$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> gives a total of roughly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/1/f11861208874b795fb1e052362140b90cb20e6a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.506\\cdot133^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"17\" />. By testing, we know that the fifth root of this value is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/67183620be1ef5d26372ed76fef5657a87b32e91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.1\\cdot133=146.3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"14\" />, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/7/24721efc79c2024775291175c207a5aa050e03e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.1^5=1.611$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"98\" height=\"17\" />, meaning we have reduced <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a1a41d9b17642e042a14d68cc42ed3a4d2b8332.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$133\\le{n}\\le{147}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" />.\nThe last digit of all four numbers, in order, are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which is gained through writing out the cycles of the last digit up to the fifth power. This means that the answer has a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, reducing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> down to either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/9/489263c8336e32dbda8c2160060f5aacb822c9e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$134$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50ff9540650f0f95f80da2f6692fc8ee413e2eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />. Since the previous cheesing shows obviously that the value is closer to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88e957a4e809e84192ed86a1413de32e999bdce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$146.3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> than it is to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/0/9501915f08ed1cf295fdd389481801277bcb2e94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$133$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, we know our final answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/4/a842c2b8241b1784706e13c86f350656b7208be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{144}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" /> is correct.\n</p><p>Cheese solution by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Juwushu\" title=\"User:Juwushu\">juwushu</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_8_.28Guesswork_or_Bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8_(Guesswork_or_Bash)\">Solution 8 (Guesswork or Bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8 (Guesswork or Bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/b/03b67436a4837cce36c8adeea278f9338f6495f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^5 \\equiv a \\pmod{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"21\" /> for all a. You can prove this later. So we know the number ends with 4. Since 133 is the biggest number, while everything else is small, we can safely assume that it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/4/a842c2b8241b1784706e13c86f350656b7208be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{144}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />, because 5th powers vary wildly. It is not 134 because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d078ea75ab260a4a108f8e6db96d1088a5850538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$110^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" /> plays a role in the sum.  We can also just take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/2/aa2799624e2457085e038b3630e595c033248ae4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$130^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> and the other numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/f/cffe65c16c7b3fa93cf5c7c3c72ef1eba1932739.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$110^5, 80^5,20^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" />, add them up, and we realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/3/443ae379ebebd05a1e44ef3403f76ecfc8c1403a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$140^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> is close to this. Then we also get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/4/a842c2b8241b1784706e13c86f350656b7208be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{144}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" /> \n</p><p>~Aarav22\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_9_.28Guess.2C_only_if_you_have_no_time.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_9_(Guess,_only_if_you_have_no_time)\">Solution 9 (Guess, only if you have no time)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 9 (Guess, only if you have no time)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number should be around 140, and since most solutions in the AIME are 'round' numbers, we can guess 144.\n~Sigma_Bob\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark\">Remark</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Remark\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We could also take this expression mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/43420adcd0fce9dce3978d53b97a8e0262b58da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> which would give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/e/7be8781a9923f5962b32449a43306a3bb38d5a29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\equiv4\\pmod{7}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" /> Then the only reasonable number that works is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/4/f64cc2ce37873d7b3313789d7822aede938779a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"17\" /> so we could safely assume this is the answer.\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Grogg007\" title=\"User:Grogg007\">grogg007</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME\" title=\"1989 AIME\">1989 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1989 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1989\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" tit